        "original_id": "1e909736-38dc-5c8e-ba26-344177d8bca3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Xinghua, Jiangsu; Taizhou; Yancheng; Yangzhou; Jingdezhen; Jiangxi; Anhui; Zhuxian; Foshan; Hankou; China\n- People: Hou Yifan\n- Roles: county-level city; prefecture-level city; chess grandmaster\n- Concepts: four ancient towns of Qing Dynasty China\n\nFacts:\n- Xinghua is a county-level city under the administration of Taizhou in Jiangsu province, China.\n- Xinghua borders Yancheng to the north and east and Yangzhou to the west.\n- Jingdezhen, also called the Town of Jingde, is a prefecture-level city in northeastern Jiangxi province, China, and it previously had town status.\n- In 2007, Jingdezhen had a total population of 1,554,000.\n- Jingdezhen borders Anhui to the north.\n- Hou Yifan was born on 27 February 1994 in Xinghua, Jiangsu, China.\n- Hou Yifan is a Chinese chess grandmaster and former chess prodigy.\n- Zhuxian, along with Foshan, Jingde, and Hankou, is regarded as one of the four ancient towns of Qing Dynasty China.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
